WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
I thought I should acknowledge

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.770
how much confusion there is right now

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.870
in the country about what
we're supposed to do.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.660
There's so much confusion
about how we should be

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.176
reacting to COVID-19,
a lot of mixed signals

00:00:14.176 --> 00:00:15.970
from public officials.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.700
The president says one thing,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.020
many governors say another thing.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.330
Even the nation's top
public health agency,

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.180
the CDC, has been inconsistent.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.320
Check it out. In March, the CDC said

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.990
we didn't have to wear masks,
now they're saying we do.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.280
Well I looked into it, and
a lot of recommendations

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.310
on the CDC's COVID-19
website are confusing.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.667
For example, check this
out, they're saying

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:42.160
"wash your hands for 20 seconds

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.807
or five seconds if no one's watching."

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.923
Look at this, if someone
sneezes near you, punch the air.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:55.060
That's yes, if you win
at Rock, Paper, Scissors,

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.173
the other person gets
the virus and you don't.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.880
You can hook up with a stranger in a bar

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.140
as long a should remain
emotionally distant.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.180
Well, I'm safe. (chuckles)

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.330
Since small children are low
risk for contracting COVID,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.750
it is acceptable to use a baby
as a protective face mask.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.410
That's wrong, I shouldn't, please,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.080
don't pay attention to that one.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.550
Run. Run and never come back.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.790
Are you listening to me?

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.483
You have to disappear.
Get outta here! Go now!

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.480
If you used your time during
quarantine to write a novel,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.840
learn Mandarin, or do anything productive,

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.993
just know that everyone hates you.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.330
Although it is only one of many reasons

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.200
not to go near clowns, please be aware

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.410
that all clowns have coronavirus.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.940
You can't get COVID in a hot tub,

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.976
or was it you can't get
pregnant? Let's say both

00:01:48.976 --> 00:01:52.160
and also my parents are
out of town this weekend.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.100
And finally, although
there's a low likelihood

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.380
of spreading COVID while
jogging without a mask,

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.970
at least put on a shirt
you (bleep) animal.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.040
Well good luck figuring those out.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.203
As I said, very confusing.

